{"availability":"available","full":"chaos-mesh/chaos-mesh","name":"chaos-mesh","description":"A Chaos Engineering Platform for Kubernetes.","category":"Other","language":"Go","stars":7929,"forks":1034,"created":"2019-09-04T02:29:38Z","updated":"2026-10-03T20:22:54Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"master","homepage":"https://chaos-mesh.org","topics":["chaos","chaos-engineering","chaos-experiments","chaos-mesh","chaos-testing","cloud-native","cncf","fault-injection","golang","kubernetes","microservices","operator","site-reliability-engineering"],"demo":"https://killercoda.com/saiyampathak/scenario/chaos-mesh","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:53.769Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:53.769Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-04T08:15:53.769Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-03T22:13:32.018Z","stars":7929,"forks":1034},{"at":"2026-10-04T08:15:53.769Z","stars":7929,"forks":1034}],"technologies":["Go"],"lastDemoCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:32.105Z","overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Chaos Mesh is an open source, cloud-native Chaos Engineering platform for Kubernetes. It uses Kubernetes custom resources to define, orchestrate, and observe controlled fault injection against workloads, infrastructure, cloud services, and applications.","Chaos Mesh is a Cloud Native Computing Foundation (CNCF) incubating project. If you are an organization that wants to help shape the evolution of technologies that are container-packaged, dynamically-scheduled and microservices-oriented, consider joining the CNCF."],"features":["Broad fault coverage: Pod, network, DNS, HTTP, I/O, time, stress, kernel, block device, JVM, physical machine, AWS, Azure, and GCP faults.","Kubernetes-native API: Chaos experiments are defined as custom resources and managed through the Kubernetes API using standard Kubernetes tooling and RBAC.","Experiment orchestration: Schedule, Workflow, and StatusCheck resources support recurring experiments, serial or parallel workflows, and application health checks.","Dashboard: create, manage, and inspect experiments, schedules, and workflows through a web UI and API.","Multi-cluster execution: manage remote clusters and dispatch supported chaos experiments from a management cluster."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chaos-mesh/chaos-mesh/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"12e3c31951491547d2efbf4a4d211aab3c15a3f8c8917e78e7cb26ba7dab85a3","extractedAt":"2026-10-03T06:15:53.252Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:32.100Z","overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T20:22:54Z","enrichmentAttemptAt":"2026-10-05T16:57:46.920Z","latestRelease":{"name":"v2.8.4","tag":"v2.8.4","publishedAt":"2026-08-18T07:27:04Z","url":"https://github.com/chaos-mesh/chaos-mesh/releases/tag/v2.8.4"},"releaseCheckedAt":"2026-10-05T16:57:46.920Z","screenshots":[{"src":"previews/048bcbde62e6eefc51cdf844.jpg","kind":"demo","capturedAt":"2026-10-04T10:38:19.093Z","url":"https://killercoda.com/saiyampathak/scenario/chaos-mesh"}],"demoHealth":{"url":"https://killercoda.com/saiyampathak/scenario/chaos-mesh","attemptedAt":"2026-10-04T10:38:19.093Z","status":"working","checkedAt":"2026-10-04T10:38:19.093Z","lastWorkingAt":"2026-10-04T10:38:19.093Z","target":"https://killercoda.com/saiyampathak/scenario/chaos-mesh","failureCount":0,"nextCheckAt":"2026-10-11T10:38:19.093Z"},"projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Chaos Mesh is an open source, cloud-native Chaos Engineering platform for Kubernetes. It uses Kubernetes custom resources to define, orchestrate, and observe controlled fault injection against workloads, infrastructure, cloud services, and applications.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chaos-mesh/chaos-mesh/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"12e3c31951491547d2efbf4a4d211aab3c15a3f8c8917e78e7cb26ba7dab85a3","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/chaos-mesh/chaos-mesh/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-03T22:13:32.101Z"},"readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sour